Subject: [PATCH] liuqin: preserve audio lifecycle across system sleep and DSP restart

Stop DSP graphs outside PCM locks before system sleep and restore SoundWire
ports before codec power-up. Disable data ports before DAPM drops their
clock votes, and reset the playback queue when ALSA prepares a suspended PCM. Retain the PRM clock provider and cancel commands
when its audio service is down; replay resource votes before clocks and card
creation. Quiesce retained consumers before their providers on service loss.
Restore LPASS pin states, SoundWire enumeration and codec state on recovery.
A recreated card starts with disconnected NOPM capture mixer paths, so reset
the surviving TX macro's per-card channel masks before UCM enables the routes.

The PM/reset ordering follows the OEM Bolero macros, SoundWire controller and
WCD938x lifecycle. Board-specific behavior uses liuqin_board_quirks(), including
ABL's replacement root identifiers. Firmware readiness and failed recovery
remain errors; unrelated codec and AUX errors are not suppressed.

OEM audio source:
https://github.com/xiaomi-sm8450-kernel/android_vendor_qcom_opensource_audio-kernel/tree/721c4fb115d50aea74a2dec9ee864bf0f12682c8

